<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1941–2011</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tiger Pataudi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi was an Indian cricketer who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s youngest Test captain in 1962, at the age of 21. Despite losing the sight of one eye in a car accident, he led India in 40 Tests and guided it to its first overseas Test series win, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> in 1968. He was the titular Nawab of Pataudi until princely titles were abolished in 1971.</p></div>
